                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a4126ec0-bbf5-3972-9962-4f2ce30e5bf8",
                                        "entry_id": "83c24005-fd84-311a-be22-6d926ee95a9f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Located or positioned out of sight; not visually apparent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "535053aa-0115-42c6-8df1-6f017701c9fa",
                                                "sense_id": "a4126ec0-bbf5-3972-9962-4f2ce30e5bf8",
                                                "text": "hidden treasure; hidden talents"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84b5b75a-4d0a-473d-9783-6f5c62b3681d",
                                                "sense_id": "a4126ec0-bbf5-3972-9962-4f2ce30e5bf8",
                                                "text": "It was the Lost Oasis, the Oasis of the vision in the sand. […] Deep-hidden in the hollow, beneath the cliffs, it lay; and round it the happy verdure spread for many a rood."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a883cff-5179-4946-b17e-1bf70bfa0934",
                                                "sense_id": "a4126ec0-bbf5-3972-9962-4f2ce30e5bf8",
                                                "text": "One of the hidden glories of Victorian engineering is proper drains. Isolating a city’s effluent and shipping it away in underground sewers has probably saved more lives than any medical procedure except vaccination."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a8e332b-71ab-3424-adfd-5b9f4458fd31",
                                        "entry_id": "83c24005-fd84-311a-be22-6d926ee95a9f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Obscure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "hidden",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb55d64b-f9ac-36db-b218-1d9d1fc240b2",
                                        "entry_id": "4a8be5fa-3681-3ab5-bff2-8b34dca730bc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A hidden answer clue; one in which the letters of the solution appear consecutively in the wordplay."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d684219-65c3-40f8-857d-ab2f149739d0",
                                                "sense_id": "cb55d64b-f9ac-36db-b218-1d9d1fc240b2",
                                                "text": "Hiddens are indicated thus; (e.g.) Grow (maraudinG ROWdies)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "078bf1d2-abeb-420e-b0e4-ce2542f5f58c",
                                                "sense_id": "cb55d64b-f9ac-36db-b218-1d9d1fc240b2",
                                                "text": "The two types of clue which everyone should aim to solve at first reading are anagrams and hiddens."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f40a7c5-bdba-4cfa-8273-8e3be39c36fd",
                                                "sense_id": "cb55d64b-f9ac-36db-b218-1d9d1fc240b2",
                                                "text": "16 of the 30 clues in this puzzle are hiddens; these are asterisked."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5e9af91b-2bc7-49bb-ba34-f1846e2511d6",
                        "source_entry_id": "87f3f4ec-91cb-34fc-a956-164778fd1f65",
                        "source_sense_id": "657328e5-24c1-38d8-aa3e-3e27bd94827f",
                        "source_sense_description": "subcultuur die zich afzet tegen de gevestigde orde",
                        "target_lang_word": "furtive",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "furtive",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b97841d0-afed-3649-b339-62f0f8f8cb33",
                                        "entry_id": "197b7e16-4fcf-33d4-a50f-d3406040f068",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a thing: done with evasive or guilty secrecy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15c6bd6f-83b7-40ca-bdca-a22c051698d0",
                                                "sense_id": "b97841d0-afed-3649-b339-62f0f8f8cb33",
                                                "text": "[…] The Defendant never vvas acknovvledged by the Sieur Harrouard’s Family, nor by that of his VVife. Thus, granting him to have been in Poſſeſſion of his Son’s Eſtate, it vvould only be a furtive and clandeſtine, not a public and avovved Poſſeſſion; and conſequently ſuch a Poſſeſſion as is incapable of founding a juſt and legal Title."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4d8d3b0-0e47-4441-a839-1dad9f6f27c8",
                                                "sense_id": "b97841d0-afed-3649-b339-62f0f8f8cb33",
                                                "text": "[T]ender cares and mild domestic Loves, / With furtive watch, pursue her [a swan] as she moves; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90fe4d3b-4d89-4f7b-8ccd-862427be533c",
                                                "sense_id": "b97841d0-afed-3649-b339-62f0f8f8cb33",
                                                "text": "I noticed the same singular, and as it were, furtive glance over the shoulder that had attracted my attention in the Cassino."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af6e2143-ec30-4448-9a8f-28c0a25e844d",
                                                "sense_id": "b97841d0-afed-3649-b339-62f0f8f8cb33",
                                                "text": "The proprietor of the house cowered over a bed-candle and a furtive tea-pot in the back drawing-room."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad8f6aa4-20a9-414c-abc3-181bfc7cd964",
                                                "sense_id": "b97841d0-afed-3649-b339-62f0f8f8cb33",
                                                "text": "\"Don't call me Solomon. Do you want to be the death of me?\" asked the man, in a furtive, frightened way."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e7ade9a-5034-47eb-9bb2-10d68814ca5d",
                                                "sense_id": "b97841d0-afed-3649-b339-62f0f8f8cb33",
                                                "text": "At the edge of my kingdom scurry / ⁠Creatures in feathers and furs— / Crows in a furtive hurry— / ⁠Hungry and cringing curs— […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77f99f83-86f1-49ef-8e60-63f03583fed0",
                                                "sense_id": "b97841d0-afed-3649-b339-62f0f8f8cb33",
                                                "text": "Actually, as Winston well knew, it was only four years since Oceania had been at war with Eastasia and in alliance with Eurasia. But that was merely a piece of furtive knowledge which he happened to possess because his memory was not satisfactorily under control."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "88dc0df5-9035-33f3-ad8e-86008cc754ef",
                                        "entry_id": "197b7e16-4fcf-33d4-a50f-d3406040f068",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a thing: that has been acquired by theft; stolen; also (generally) taken stealthily."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6302eb8d-54de-4bd0-ac5f-96cb329dec70",
                                                "sense_id": "88dc0df5-9035-33f3-ad8e-86008cc754ef",
                                                "text": "Novv ſhine theſe Planets vvith ſubſtantial Rays? / Does innate Luſtre gild their meaſur'd Days? / Or do they (as your Schemes, I think, have ſhovvn) / Dart furtive Beams, and Glory not their ovvn, / All Servants to that Source of Light, the Sun?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "62b3dbf3-991d-3d71-a23f-4b366e89ea31",
                                        "entry_id": "197b7e16-4fcf-33d4-a50f-d3406040f068",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a person or an animal: sly, stealthy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "205a9ee2-c53f-4e0d-a4b7-b57050c5694a",
                                                "sense_id": "62b3dbf3-991d-3d71-a23f-4b366e89ea31",
                                                "text": "All women have their foibles. Wise husbands must bear and forbear. Is that all? wherefore, then, is her aspect so furtive, wherefore on his a wild, vigilant sternness?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30090df7-2f0c-4ede-be1d-87db64d452f1",
                                                "sense_id": "62b3dbf3-991d-3d71-a23f-4b366e89ea31",
                                                "text": "So, Riderhood looking after him as he went, and he with his furtive hand laid upon the dagger as he passed it, and his eyes upon the boat, were much upon a par."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da5976d2-b294-4b90-a17e-8d4ea17a4258",
                                                "sense_id": "62b3dbf3-991d-3d71-a23f-4b366e89ea31",
                                                "text": "Gluttonous, hoarding jay; he should have hedge-hopped and lurched from tree to tree in his usual furtive manner."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d9d55913-431d-3a24-9f78-7dc2185bafc0",
                                        "entry_id": "197b7e16-4fcf-33d4-a50f-d3406040f068",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a person, etc.: inclined to steal; pilfering, thieving."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
